---
description: Turn the exam task into a requirements checklist and a small plan (no code yet)
---

# Plan the task

Use the task text the user provides with this command (or ask for it if missing).

1. Do NOT write code yet.
2. Create `REQUIREMENTS.md` with a numbered checklist copied from the exact wording of the task.
3. Add an "Assumptions" section: every ambiguity and the assumption you propose.
4. Propose a plan of at most 8 steps. Step 1 must be the smallest end-to-end slice (one item, input to output).
5. List the libraries you will use (only requests, selenium, pytest and the standard library unless the task says otherwise).
6. Stop and wait for the user to approve the plan.
